  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186129154,
      "id": "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443",
      "title": "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "db8cf3b8-5bd2-5948-ad45-7ae6d23b89fd",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/9a4d84877a893ed1fd06ae4d2896c2ef49258140dee236a74d333f263b133cbe.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=-3$ is a simple root.\n- **II.** $x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n- **III.** $x=3$ is a root of even multiplicity.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The root $x=-3$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the \n$x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement II is true. The root $x=0$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement III is true. The root $x=3$ has an even multiplicity because at $x=3$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "5538f3b7-0c92-5049-8bbe-aaf93448e886",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
